HST Office: HST Sheets has GROUPBY and PIVOTBY (owner decision 2026-11-14: the whole LAMBDA family is in 1.0.2).
Upstream LibreOffice has neither; this is HST code on the callable machinery of hst-sheets-lambda-functions.patch.

- GROUPBY(row_fields; values; function; [field_headers]; [total_depth]; [sort_order]; [filter_array];
  [field_relationship]) and PIVOTBY(row_fields; col_fields; values; function; [field_headers]; [row_total_depth];
  [row_sort_order]; [col_total_depth]; [col_sort_order]; [filter_array]; [relative_to]).
- function is a built-in function passed as a value (SUM, AVERAGE, COUNTA, MAX, PERCENTOF, ARRAYTOTEXT...) or a
  LAMBDA; it gets one group's values as a one-column array. A function with two required parameters
  (PERCENTOF, LAMBDA(x;y;...)) also gets the values it is relative to: for GROUPBY all filtered values of that
  column, for PIVOTBY per relative_to (0 column totals, 1 row totals, 2 grand total, 3 parent column total,
  4 parent row total).
- field_headers 0/1/2/3 (omitted: headers when the first values row is text and the second a number);
  generated headers read "Row Field n" / "Value n". total_depth 0, 1 grand total "Total" (default), 2 with
  subtotals, -1/-2 at the top. sort_order: 1-based column indexes, negative descending; a value column sorts
  each level by the group aggregate; default ascending keys (numbers, text, logical values, errors, blanks;
  text case-insensitive). field_relationship 1 (table) groups by all fields at once without subtotals.
  filter_array: a column of logical values. An error from the function stays in its own cell.
- PIVOTBY layout: column keys on top (one row per column field, "Total" for column totals), a value-name row
  when there are several value columns or headers are shown, row keys on the left; empty intersections stay
  empty. Known differences: the reference application returns #CALC! where this gives #VALUE! (no data
  left, an argument out of range); its header-row layout for shown headers may differ in detail.
- .xlsx: _xlfn.GROUPBY/_xlfn.PIVOTBY; a function passed as a value is written _xleta.SUM (_xleta.PERCENTOF,
  without _xlfn.) as the reference application does, and _xleta.PERCENTOF is read back as PERCENTOF. ODF:
  COM.MICROSOFT.GROUPBY / COM.MICROSOFT.PIVOTBY.
- Function Wizard: up to 11 parameters (ScFuncDescCore optional-argument flags and the parameter class table
  grow from 7 to 11); English and Vietnamese text.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sc_excelcompat_functions_test (testGroupByPivotByAndLambda: results, XLSX and ODS round trip;
testLambdaCommonFormsXlsx: MAP, BYROW, GROUPBY as array formulas, REDUCE, LET with a LAMBDA, XLSX round trip),
tests/unit/test_sheets_groupby_pivotby.py, tests/runtime/check-sheets-excel-functions.py.
